From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Chang <jonathan.chang@centron.tw>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 21:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] realtek: boot to rescue mode when install button is pressed

CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM (GPIO 26) is wired to the front-panel install
button on the Centron boards (active low). misc_init_r() already requests
and reads that line for the "usb-boot-key" feature, so re-requesting it
from common/autoboot.c fails with -EBUSY.

Instead of adding a second consumer, handle the button where the line is
already owned: when it is held down at power-on, override bootcfg with
"#rescue" so boot_yocto boots the installer / rescue FIT configuration.
This is the same end result as running altbootcmd.

The install button is a rescue trigger, not a USB-boot jumper on this
hardware, so it no longer sets boot_usb.

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Chang <jonathan.chang@centron.tw>
---
 arch/arm/mach-realtek/board.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-realtek/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-realtek/board.c
--- a/arch/arm/mach-realtek/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-realtek/board.c
@@ -304,6 +304,13 @@ int misc_init_r(void)
 	gpio_request(CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM, "usb-boot-key");
 	gpio_direction_input(CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM);
-	if (!gpio_get_value(CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM))
-	env_set("boot_usb", "1");
+	/*
+	 * Centron: CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM (GPIO 26) is wired to the
+	 * front-panel install button (active low). When it is held down
+	 * at power-on, force the "#rescue" FIT configuration so that
+	 * boot_yocto boots the installer / rescue image instead of the
+	 * normal one. Same end result as running altbootcmd.
+	 */
+	if (!gpio_get_value(CONFIG_USB_BOOT_GPIO_NUM))
+		env_set("bootcfg", "#rescue");
 #endif
 #endif /* USB_STORAGE */

